@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+type: decision
+status: active
+updated: 2026-11-06
+sources: [.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md, .harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md, commits 4d9b627 3556e27 0be020e 3bd6c55 868d83c 8f1b148]
+verified_by: tests/gate.test.sh (tests/gate-denied.list loop)
+---
+# 0012: Gate shrink: keep the gate, trim it to observed use
+
+**Context.** The 4b item in [0005](0005-gate-only-inside-herdr.md) left "shrink the parser toward `permissions` rules" as a separate design. The analyst's `.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md` replayed 881 conductor Bash calls from 8 transcripts (2026-10-18..28) through the 552-line gate: 754 allowed, 127 denied (106 of those from two ungated daemon-env sessions). Never used: `git show --stat`; `herdr status`, `pane list|layout`, `workspace|tab list`; `gh issue|run|repo view|auth|browse`, `pr status`; jq as a pipe consumer (0 allowed). Chaining was 44 of 754 (5.8%), pipes 0, `2>&1` 0. No filesystem MCP server was configured.
+
+**Decision.**
+- Trimmed to what was used: `gh pr create|view|list|checks|comment|edit|merge` only (`--body-file` from `.harness/` or `docs/`, no `merge -d`, no `api`); `git branch` list-only (`-a -r -v --show-current`); `herdr pane get|current`; no jq. Chained commands, pipes and redirects are denied by a quote-aware single-command scanner (wiki: conductor-shell-one-command).
+- Agent/Workflow/Monitor/NotebookEdit and `mcp__filesystem__*` cases were dropped from the gate; the conductor frontmatter `disallowedTools` removes the four tools (pinned by a gate test), and the hook matcher is `Edit|Write|Read|Grep|Glob|Bash`.
+- The gate keys on hook `agent_type` (not env), closing the daemon-inherits-worker-env hole.
+- Kept: the path helpers (`rel`/`physrel`/`physical`, readable/writable, raw-stream block; ~109 lines) and the Bash allowlist. They are the symlink and raw-stream protection; a 50-line gate is not possible without dropping symlink resolution, Glob/Grep scoping and the allowlist.
+- `tests/gate-denied.list` (deny probes plus 5 allow controls) is looped by the gate suite so each trim is checked.
+- Rejected, option f (`permissions` rules instead of the gate): user-scope `permissions` also bind workers (same settings file), deny beats allow so "deny Read except .harness/docs" cannot be written, and only tool-name denies are expressible, which `disallowedTools` already covers.
+- Rejected, B′ (native subagents instead of the harness runner, `.harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md`, 2026-11-03): subagents die when the conductor exits ("1 local agent couldn't be moved and was stopped"). The detached runner stays, so the gate stays.
+
+**Status.** Active. Supersedes the 4b consequence of 0005 ("shrinking toward `permissions` rules is a separate design"). Gate size 552 → 513 lines; the deny/allow tables sit together near the top of the script.
+
+**Consequences.** A new tool the conductor should use must be added to the allowlist (and `conductor.md`, "You may run directly") in the same change. A filesystem MCP server added later is not blocked by the gate; add it to `disallowedTools`. Prune step 5 also removed the `--via` no-op: `harness ask … --via x` is now a usage error (exit 1).
